WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:02.067
-Welcome back, everyone.

00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:04.000
We're talking to Ariana DeBose
right here.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.801 --> 00:00:08.200
Now, you're hosting
"Saturday Night Live"
this weekend.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:10.634
But let's talk
"West Side Story."

00:00:10.634 --> 00:00:12.534
Man, oh, man,
I think this is --

00:00:12.534 --> 00:00:15.000
Yeah, you are phenomenal in it.
-Thank you.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.734
-I think you got nominated
for over 40 awards or something.

00:00:17.734 --> 00:00:19.601
-It's wild.
-It's wild, right?

00:00:19.601 --> 00:00:21.501
But congrats.

00:00:21.501 --> 00:00:25.534
When you get the call to do --
is it like,

00:00:25.534 --> 00:00:28.400
"Hey, Steven Spielberg wants
to meet you for his new movie"?

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:30.801
Or do you know that
it's "West Wide" or what's...?

00:00:30.801 --> 00:00:33.300
-No, I was doing "Summer,"

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:34.734
the Donna Summer musical,
at the time.

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:36.701
I was singing -- ♪ oh, no ♪
eight times a week.

00:00:36.701 --> 00:00:38.868
-That's right.
-And I was really tired

00:00:38.868 --> 00:00:40.200
one evening after the show,

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:41.934
and Cindy Tolan,
the casting director, called,

00:00:41.934 --> 00:00:44.267
and she goes, "Hey,
can you come to Brooklyn

00:00:44.267 --> 00:00:45.601
tomorrow at 10:00 a.m.?"

00:00:45.601 --> 00:00:48.567
And I was like, "But it's, like,
11:30 p.m. eight now."

00:00:48.567 --> 00:00:52.334
-You're like -- ♪ oh, no ♪
-♪ Oh, no ♪

00:00:52.334 --> 00:00:53.767
And she was like,
"No, just come."

00:00:53.767 --> 00:00:56.400
And I was like, "Great.
So can I just dance and sing?"

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.634
And she was like,
"Sure, sure, sure. I got you."

00:00:58.634 --> 00:01:03.534
So I get there the next day,
and I walk into the room,

00:01:03.534 --> 00:01:07.033
and there's Steven Spielberg
and Tony Kushner.

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:09.367
And I was like, "Hmm."
[ Imitates explosion ]

00:01:09.367 --> 00:01:10.767
-Wow.

00:01:10.767 --> 00:01:13.067
-And I said,
"Am I gonna do this right now?

00:01:13.067 --> 00:01:15.033
I'm gonna do this right now.
Okay."

00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:17.467
So I danced for him,
and he really liked my dancing,

00:01:17.467 --> 00:01:18.868
and then he said,
"Will you sing?"

00:01:18.868 --> 00:01:20.367
And I was like, "Sure."

00:01:20.367 --> 00:01:22.968
And I then I sing for him,
and he really likes my singing.

00:01:22.968 --> 00:01:24.467
He was like, "Great."

00:01:24.467 --> 00:01:27.234
And I said --
He said, "Will you read?"

00:01:27.234 --> 00:01:28.901
And I said, "No."

00:01:28.901 --> 00:01:30.467
-[ Laughter ]
-What?

00:01:30.467 --> 00:01:32.968
-And he said, "No?"

00:01:32.968 --> 00:01:35.834
And I was like, "No, sir."

00:01:35.834 --> 00:01:37.100
-You don't say "no"
to Steven Spielberg.

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:40.701
-I -- I realize that, but...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.701 --> 00:01:42.901
No, I had said the night before.
I was like -- Look.

00:01:42.901 --> 00:01:46.334
These scenes -- Like, these are
Tony Kushner expanded scenes.

00:01:46.334 --> 00:01:48.067
They can be wordy.
-You gotta nail it.

00:01:48.067 --> 00:01:49.968
-And they're important.
You gotta nail it.

00:01:49.968 --> 00:01:52.267
And quite frankly I'm not in the
business of going in a room

00:01:52.267 --> 00:01:53.834
as a Black woman
and not getting it right.

00:01:53.834 --> 00:01:55.167
You got to come in prepared.

00:01:55.167 --> 00:01:56.501
And I was just like,
"I'm going to tell him no,

00:01:56.501 --> 00:01:58.067
but I'd love to come back."

00:01:58.067 --> 00:02:00.634
And so he -- the -- Literally,
that was his next question

00:02:00.634 --> 00:02:03.501
after I couldn't get the rest
of my declarative statement out.

00:02:03.501 --> 00:02:04.734
-Wow.
-And, uh --

00:02:04.734 --> 00:02:06.767
-Good for you.
-He said, "Will you come back?"

00:02:06.767 --> 00:02:07.934
And I said, "I'd be honored."

00:02:07.934 --> 00:02:09.534
And then, you know,
a couple weeks later,

00:02:09.534 --> 00:02:14.000
he called me in a nail salon,
with the foils on my nails.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.467
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.467 --> 00:02:18.234
And he said, "Hi. It's Steven.
I'm on an airplane."

00:02:18.234 --> 00:02:20.868
I was like, "That is so great.
Um, one second."

00:02:20.868 --> 00:02:22.534
-"Guys, Steven Spielberg's
on the phone!

00:02:22.534 --> 00:02:25.601
Can everyone just quiet down?
It's happening."

00:02:25.601 --> 00:02:28.434
-"Quit that drying over there."
-"This is real over here."

00:02:28.434 --> 00:02:31.100
-And he asked me
if I would be his Anita.

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:32.834
And I was like -- [ Gasping ]
-You're Anita.

00:02:32.834 --> 00:02:34.534
And you got the biggest song
in the movie.

00:02:34.534 --> 00:02:36.033
-Yeah, crazy, crazy.
-"America."

00:02:36.033 --> 00:02:37.434
-I can't --
-Are you serious?

00:02:37.434 --> 00:02:38.801
-I can't believe it.

00:02:38.801 --> 00:02:41.701
-It's gorgeous, by the way.
-Thank you.

00:02:41.701 --> 00:02:44.367
-It is --
What was it like on set?

00:02:44.367 --> 00:02:45.934
I mean, is it --
-Oh, it's wild.

00:02:45.934 --> 00:02:50.601
I mean, Steven Spielberg sets
are huge.

00:02:50.601 --> 00:02:52.801
-The wardrobe is great.
The choreography.

00:02:52.801 --> 00:02:56.300
-Everything! I mean,
Paul Tazewell's costumes.

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:58.501
It's like a color explosion.
-It's amazing.

00:02:58.501 --> 00:03:01.634
-But I kid you not --
it's like going to summer camp,

00:03:01.634 --> 00:03:03.968
and Steven and Tony
are your camp counselors.

00:03:03.968 --> 00:03:05.868
And, you know --
-Wow.

00:03:05.868 --> 00:03:07.901
-We finished like six days
of "Dance at the Gym,"

00:03:07.901 --> 00:03:10.901
and I'm really tired
and I'm eating a Pop-Tart,

00:03:10.901 --> 00:03:13.868
And Steven's like
"Addie. What is that?"

00:03:13.868 --> 00:03:15.701
And I said, "It's a Pop-Tart.
Are you judging me?"

00:03:15.701 --> 00:03:18.334
And he was like, "No.
What flavor are you eating?"

00:03:18.334 --> 00:03:21.200
And I said, "Cinnamon sugar."

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.234
-Ooh. Okay.

00:03:23.234 --> 00:03:25.400
-"Brittany, can I get
a strawberry Pop-Tart?!"

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:27.167
-No way.
-I kid you not.

00:03:27.167 --> 00:03:28.701
It's summer camp.

00:03:28.701 --> 00:03:30.100
-Wow. You bonded over Pop-Tarts?

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:32.300
-Over Pop-Tarts. It was great.
-See, he's a smart dude.

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:33.868
I love Steven Spielberg.
I -- Yeah.

00:03:33.868 --> 00:03:35.234
He toast his?
-He eats Pop-Tarts.

00:03:35.234 --> 00:03:36.834
-You ever do them raw?

00:03:36.834 --> 00:03:40.067
-I'm a raw Pop-Tart girl.
-Me too! I'm a raw!

00:03:40.067 --> 00:03:43.334
I'm a sushi Pop-Tart...
-Hey! [ Laughs ]

00:03:43.334 --> 00:03:46.133
-Me too. Me too.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:03:46.133 --> 00:03:49.501
Here's Ariana DeBose performing
"America" in "West Side Story."

00:03:49.501 --> 00:03:51.033
Take a look at this.

00:03:51.033 --> 00:04:00.501
♪♪

00:04:00.501 --> 00:04:09.901
♪♪

00:04:09.901 --> 00:04:13.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:15.200
-Ariana DeBose!

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:17.667
"West Side Story"
is in theaters now.

00:04:17.667 --> 00:04:20.467
Catch her this weekend
hosting "Saturday Night Live,"

00:04:20.467 --> 00:04:22.300
with musical guest Bleachers.

